  "pacific-atlantic-water-flow": {
    "title": "Pacific Atlantic Water Flow",
    "leetcodeId": 417,
    "content": [
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          "There is an ",
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "m x n"
            ]
          },
          " rectangular island that borders both the ",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Pacific Ocean"
            ]
          },
          " and ",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Atlantic Ocean"
            ]
          },
          ". The ",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Pacific Ocean"
            ]
          },
          " touches the island's left and top edges, and the ",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Atlantic Ocean"
            ]
          },
          " touches the island's right and bottom edges."
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          "The island is partitioned into a grid of square cells. You are given an ",
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "m x n"
            ]
          },
          " integer matrix ",
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "heights"
            ]
          },
          " where ",
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "heights[r][c]"
            ]
          },
          " represents the ",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "height above sea level"
            ]
          },
          " of the cell at coordinate ",
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "(r, c)"
            ]
          },
          "."
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          "The island receives a lot of rain, and the rain water can flow to neighboring cells directly north, south, east, and west if the neighboring cell's height is ",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "less than or equal to"
            ]
          },
          " the current cell's height. Water can flow from any cell adjacent to an ocean into the ocean."
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          "Return ",
          {
            "tag": "em",
            "children": [
              "a ",
              {
                "tag": "strong",
                "children": [
                  "2D list"
                ]
              },
              " of grid coordinates "
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "result"
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "em",
            "children": [
              " where "
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "result[i] = [r",
              {
                "tag": "sub",
                "children": [
                  "i"
                ]
              },
              ", c",
              {
                "tag": "sub",
                "children": [
                  "i"
                ]
              },
              "]"
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "em",
            "children": [
              " denotes that rain water can flow from cell "
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "code",
            "children": [
              "(r",
              {
                "tag": "sub",
                "children": [
                  "i"
                ]
              },
              ", c",
              {
                "tag": "sub",
                "children": [
                  "i"
                ]
              },
              ")"
            ]
          },
          {
            "tag": "em",
            "children": [
              " to ",
              {
                "tag": "strong",
                "children": [
                  "both"
                ]
              },
              " the Pacific and Atlantic oceans"
            ]
          },
          "."
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          " "
        ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Example 1:"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
        "tag": "img",
        "src": "assets/problem-statements/59df7bbe1ff4303c.jpg",
        "alt": "Example illustration",
        "width": 400
      },
      "\n",
      {
        "tag": "pre",
        "children": [
          "\n",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Input:"
            ]
          },
          " heights = [[1,2,2,3,5],[3,2,3,4,4],[2,4,5,3,1],[6,7,1,4,5],[5,1,1,2,4]]\n",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Output:"
            ]
          },
          " [[0,4],[1,3],[1,4],[2,2],[3,0],[3,1],[4,0]]\n",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Explanation:"
            ]
          },
          " The following cells can flow to the Pacific and Atlantic oceans, as shown below:\n[0,4]: [0,4] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [0,4] -> Atlantic Ocean\n[1,3]: [1,3] -> [0,3] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [1,3] -> [1,4] -> Atlantic Ocean\n[1,4]: [1,4] -> [1,3] -> [0,3] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [1,4] -> Atlantic Ocean\n[2,2]: [2,2] -> [1,2] -> [0,2] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [2,2] -> [2,3] -> [2,4] -> Atlantic Ocean\n[3,0]: [3,0] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [3,0] -> [4,0] -> Atlantic Ocean\n[3,1]: [3,1] -> [3,0] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [3,1] -> [4,1] -> Atlantic Ocean\n[4,0]: [4,0] -> Pacific Ocean \n       [4,0] -> Atlantic Ocean\nNote that there are other possible paths for these cells to flow to the Pacific and Atlantic oceans.\n"
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Example 2:"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "pre",
        "children": [
          "\n",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Input:"
            ]
          },
          " heights = [[1]]\n",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Output:"
            ]
          },
          " [[0,0]]\n",
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Explanation:"
            ]
          },
          " The water can flow from the only cell to the Pacific and Atlantic oceans.\n"
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          " "
        ]
      },
      "\n",
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "children": [
          {
            "tag": "strong",
            "children": [
              "Constraints:"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "\n\n",
      {
        "tag": "ul",
        "children": [
          "\n\t",
          {
            "tag": "li",
            "children": [
              {
                "tag": "code",
                "children": [
                  "m == heights.length"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "\n\t",
          {
            "tag": "li",
            "children": [
              {
                "tag": "code",
                "children": [
                  "n == heights[r].length"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "\n\t",
          {
            "tag": "li",
            "children": [
              {
                "tag": "code",
                "children": [
                  "1 <= m, n <= 200"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "\n\t",
          {
            "tag": "li",
            "children": [
              {
                "tag": "code",
                "children": [
                  "0 <= heights[r][c] <= 10",
                  {
                    "tag": "sup",
                    "children": [
                      "5"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "\n"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "sourceUrl": "https://leetcode.com/problems/pacific-atlantic-water-flow/",
    "mirrorUrl": "https://github.com/doocs/leetcode/blob/e0ee4994e85b6cd091149b79bd62785311193726/solution/0400-0499/0417.Pacific%20Atlantic%20Water%20Flow/README_EN.md"
  },
